character -- compute characters of finite group action
******************************************************

Description
===========

Use this method to compute the Betti characters of a finite group action on a
minimal free resolution or the characters of a finite group action on the
components of a graded module. See the specific use cases for more details.

All characters are bigraded by homological degree and internal degree
(inherited from the complex or module they are computed from). Modules are
considered to be concentrated in homological degree zero.

Characters may also be constructed by hand using *note
character(PolynomialRing,HashTable):
character_lpPolynomialRing_cmHashTable_rp,.

* Menu:

* Character::                   the class of all characters of finite group representations
* character(ActionOnComplex): character_lpActionOnComplex_rp.  compute all Betti characters of minimal free resolution
* character(ActionOnComplex,ZZ): character_lpActionOnComplex_cmZZ_rp.  compute Betti characters of minimal free resolution
* character(ActionOnGradedModule,List): character_lpActionOnGradedModule_cmList_rp.  compute characters of graded components of a module
* character(PolynomialRing,HashTable): character_lpPolynomialRing_cmHashTable_rp.  construct a character
* character(CharacterDecomposition,CharacterTable): character_lpCharacterDecomposition_cmCharacterTable_rp.  recover character from decomposition

Ways to use character:
======================

  * *note character(ActionOnComplex): character_lpActionOnComplex_rp, --
    compute all Betti characters of minimal free resolution
  * *note character(ActionOnComplex,ZZ): character_lpActionOnComplex_cmZZ_rp,
    -- compute Betti characters of minimal free resolution
  * *note character(ActionOnGradedModule,List):
    character_lpActionOnGradedModule_cmList_rp, -- compute characters of graded
    components of a module
  * "character(ActionOnGradedModule,ZZ)" -- see *note
    character(ActionOnGradedModule,List):
    character_lpActionOnGradedModule_cmList_rp, -- compute characters of graded
    components of a module
  * "character(ActionOnGradedModule,ZZ,ZZ)" -- see *note
    character(ActionOnGradedModule,List):
    character_lpActionOnGradedModule_cmList_rp, -- compute characters of graded
    components of a module
  * *note character(CharacterDecomposition,CharacterTable):
    character_lpCharacterDecomposition_cmCharacterTable_rp, -- recover
    character from decomposition
  * *note character(PolynomialRing,HashTable):
    character_lpPolynomialRing_cmHashTable_rp, -- construct a character

For the programmer
==================

The object *note character: character, is a *note method function with options:
(Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunctionWithOptions,.

