Equality checks -- compare actions and characters
*************************************************

Use == to check if two actions, characters, decompositions or tables are equal.

For actions, the underlying ring and object (complex or module) must be the
same. The group elements used to set up the actions being compared must be the
same and in the same order. In the case of actions on complexes, the ==
operator compares the group action in all homological degrees. In the case of
actions on modules, the == operator compares the group action on the module
generators.

For characters, the underlying ring must be the same (see *note Character
class: Character class,), as well as the degree orbit and representative
functions (see *note Semidirect: Semidirect,). Characters are compared across
all homological and internal degrees.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x_1..x_4]                                                        |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = R                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal apply(subsets(gens R, 2), product)                            |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = ideal (x x , x x , x x , x x , x x , x x )                              |
|             1 2   1 3   2 3   1 4   2 4   3 4                               |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : Ideal of R                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : RI = res I                                                              |
|                                                                             |
|      1      6      8      3                                                 |
|o3 = R  <-- R  <-- R  <-- R                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|     0      1      2      3                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : Complex                                                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : S4 = symmetricGroupActors(R)                                            |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = {| x_2 x_3 x_4 x_1 |, | x_2 x_3 x_1 x_4 |, | x_2 x_1 x_4 x_3 |, | x_2   |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     x_1 x_3 x_4 |, | x_1 x_2 x_3 x_4 |}                                     |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : A = action(RI,S4)                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = Complex with 5 actors                                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o5 : ActionOnComplex                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : G = {map(RI_3, RI_3, {{0, -1, 1}, {1, 1, 0}, {0, 1, 0}}),               |
|          map(RI_3, RI_3, {{0, 1, 0}, {-1, -1, 0}, {0, -1, 1}}),             |
|          map(RI_3, RI_3, {{0, -1, 1}, {-1, 0, -1}, {0, 0, -1}}),            |
|          map(RI_3, RI_3, {{0, 1, 0}, {1, 0, 0}, {0, 0, -1}}),               |
|          map(RI_3, RI_3, {{1, 0, 0}, {0, 1, 0}, {0, 0, 1}}) }               |
|                                                                             |
|o6 = {{4} | 0 -1 1 |, {4} | 0  1  0 |, {4} | 0  -1 1  |, {4} | 0 1 0  |, {4} |
|      {4} | 1 1  0 |  {4} | -1 -1 0 |  {4} | -1 0  -1 |  {4} | 1 0 0  |  {4} |
|      {4} | 0 1  0 |  {4} | 0  -1 1 |  {4} | 0  0  -1 |  {4} | 0 0 -1 |  {4} |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     | 1 0 0 |}                                                              |
|     | 0 1 0 |                                                               |
|     | 0 0 1 |                                                               |
|                                                                             |
|o6 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : B = action(RI,S4,G,3)                                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o7 = Complex with 5 actors                                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o7 : ActionOnComplex                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : A == B                                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o8 = true                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : character A == character B                                              |
|                                                                             |
|o9 = true                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
