Nagel, A. O'Keefe, T. Römer, A. Seceleanu - Betti numbers of symmetric shifted
ideals (see https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jalgebra.2020.04.037 ) uses
representations induced from products of smaller symmetric groups. To compare
that description with the results obtained here, one may use the
Littlewood-Richardson rule to decompose induced representations into a direct
sum of irreducibles.





