module in homological degree two in the resolution of the defining ideal of the
Klein configuration is a direct sum of two trivial representations, one in
degree 11 and one in degree 13. It follows that its second exterior power is a
trivial representation concentrated in degree 24. As observed in the second
proof of Proposition 8.1 in BDHHSS (see https://doi.org/10.1093/imrn/rnx329 ),
