BettiCharacters Example 4 -- a multigraded example
**************************************************

Consider the polynomial ring $\mathbb{Q} [x_1,x_2,y_1,y_2,y_3]$ with the
variables $x_i$ of bidegree {1,0} and the variables $y_j$ of bidegree {0,1}. We
consider the action of a product of two symmetric groups, the first permuting
the $x_i$ variables and the second permuting the $y_j$ variables. We compute
the Betti characters of this group on the resolution of the bigraded irrelevant
ideal $\langle x_1,x_2\rangle \cap \langle y_1,y_2,y_3\rangle$. This is also
the edge ideal of the complete bipartite graph $K_{2,3}$.

