entries. This results in $\mathfrak{S}_3$ acting on the grading group
$\mathbb{Z}^3$ (the character group of $(\Bbbk^\times)^3$) by permuting the
entries of the degree vectors. Thus, the orbit of a degree $d\in \mathbb{Z}^3$
consists of all permutations of $d$; we fix the nonincreasing permutation of
$d$ as the distinguished representative of this orbit. See *note Semidirect:
Semidirect, for details.

